{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" or render_mode == "dialogue_target" %}
{# Limbs this actor lost in a fight and lives without (survivable dismemberment, LivingDismember.h). #}
{% if actorUUID and actorUUID != 0 %}
{% if render_mode == "dialogue_target" %}
{% set missing_seen = sever_missing_limb_seen(actorUUID) %}
{% if missing_seen != "" %}
{% set actor = decnpc(actorUUID) %}
## Visible Wounds
{{ actor.name }} {{ missing_seen }}.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
{% set missing_limb = sever_missing_limb(actorUUID) %}
{% if missing_limb != "" %}
## Lost Limb
{{ missing_limb }}
It changes what you can do and how you carry yourself. How you feel about it, and about whoever did it (pain, shock, grief, rage, fear or a grim acceptance), depends on who you are. Never speak or act as if the limb were still there.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
